safeshell for Debian
--------------------

After installing, each user runs once:

    safeshell install

which adds a small hook to ~/.bashrc or ~/.zshrc. Open a new terminal and every
command you press Enter on is checked first. Remove it with `safeshell uninstall`.

The command is called `safeshell` (not `ss`) because /usr/bin/ss belongs to iproute2.

Sandbox on Ubuntu 24.04 and later
  The kernel setting that restricts unprivileged user namespaces stops the
  sandbox from working for unconfined programs. This package ships an AppArmor
  profile for /usr/bin/safeshell that allows exactly this one program to use
  them. `safeshell doctor` shows what your machine supports.

Optional AI
  Nothing is downloaded when the package is installed. `safeshell ai setup`
  (or /models inside the terminal) downloads a pinned, checksum-verified
  llama.cpp engine and a model into your own home directory, only after you
  ask. Cloud models (Claude, GPT, Gemini) use your own API key.

